verses.text:
Rise up, Yahweh! Save me, my God!
For you hit all my enemies on the cheek;
the teeth of the wicked you break.

Answer me when I call, God of my righteousness;
in distress you relieve me.
Be gracious to me and hear my prayer.

For there is no firmness in his mouth;
their inward being is destruction.
An open tomb is their throat;
their tongue they make smooth.

let my enemy pursue my soul and overtake it,
and let him trample my life to the ground
and cause my honor to live in the dust. Selah

His ways endure at every time;
your judgments are high from in front of him;
as for all his enemies, he snorts at them.

He ambushes in a secret place like a lion in cover;
he ambushes to seize the afflicted.
He seizes the afflicted by pulling in his net.

You have seen! Indeed, you notice mischief and vexation to take it in your hand.
The helpless person entrusts himself to you;
as for the orphan you, even you, are his helper.

For behold, the wicked, they bend a bow;
they have set their arrow on the string
to shoot in the darkness at the upright of heart.

Yahweh is in his holy temple;
Yahweh is in the heavens, his throne.
His eyes see, his eyelids test the sons of man.

Man, they speak falsehood with his neighbor;
they speak with lip of smoothness,
with a heart and a heart.

Now I know that Yahweh saves his anointed;
he will answer him from his holy heaven
with mighty deeds of salvation of his right hand.

“Roll to Yahweh;
let him deliver him.
Let him rescue him, since he delights in him.”

For dogs have surrounded me;
a company of ones doing evil have encircled me,
like the lion, my hands and my feet.

All of the fat of the earth will eat and will bow down;
to his face will kneel all of the ones going down to the dust,
even his self he kept not alive.

Even though I walk through the valley of deep darkness,
I will fear no evil, for you are with me;
your rod and your staff, they comfort me.

You arrange a table before my face in front of my enemies;
you have anointed my head with oil;
my cup overflows.

My God, in you I trust;
do not let me have shame;
do not let my enemies exult over me.

Lead me in your truth and teach me,
for you are the God of my salvation;
on you I wait all the day.

Do not remember the sins of my youth or my transgressions;
according to your covenant faithfulness remember me,
for the sake of your goodness, Yahweh!

Yahweh is my light and my salvation;
whom will I fear?
Yahweh is the refuge of my life;
whom will I dread?

For in the day of trouble he will hide me in his hut;
he will hide me in the hiding-place of his tent.
He will lift me high upon a rock.

Do not give me up to the desire of my adversaries,
for false witnesses have risen against me,
and a witness of violence.

Yahweh is my strength and my shield;
in him my heart trusts, and I am helped;
therefore my heart exults,
and with my song I will praise him.

Yahweh, you have brought up my soul from Sheol;
you have kept me alive from the ones
going down to the pit.

Yahweh, by your favor
you have made my mountain stand strong;
you hid your face, and I was dismayed.

You have turned for me my mourning to dancing;
you have loosed my sackcloth
and have clothed me with gladness

In you, Yahweh, I take refuge;
do not ever let me have shame;
in your righteousness deliver me.

Incline your ear to me; rescue me quickly;
be for me a rocky summit of refuge,
a dwelling place of strongholds to save me.

I will be glad and rejoice in your covenant faithfulness,
for you have seen my affliction;
you have known the troubles of my soul,

You are a hiding place for me;
you preserve me from distress;
you will surround me with shouts of deliverance. Selah

Do not be like a horse or like a mule which are without understanding;
ornament of him to curb with bit and bridle,
or else they will not come near to you.

But I, when they were sick, my clothing was sackcloth;
I afflicted my soul with fasting,
and my prayer returned upon my bosom.

But at my stumbling they rejoiced and gathered together;
they gathered together against me, the stricken ones, and I did not know.
They tore and did not cease.

He devises iniquity on his bed;
he stations himself on the not-good road;
he does not reject evil.

Your righteousness is like the mountains of God;
your judgments are the great deep.
You save man and beast, Yahweh.

For the wicked will perish,
and the enemies of Yahweh will be like the precious of pastures;
they vanish, in smoke they vanish.

And Yahweh helps them and delivers them;
he delivers them from the wicked and saves them,
because they have taken refuge in him.

I was mute with silence;
I was silent from good,
and my pain was stirred up.

My heart became hot within me;
in my sighing, fire burned.
I spoke with my tongue:

And he brought me up from the pit of tumult,
from the mud of the mire,
and he set my feet on a rock;
he established my steps.

I have proclaimed righteousness in the great assembly;
behold, I will not restrain my lips.
Yahweh, you, you know.

You, Yahweh, will not withhold your compassion from me;
your covenant faithfulness and your trustworthiness
will continually preserve me.

Let all the seekers of you
rejoice and be glad in you;
let the lovers of your salvation say continually,
“May Yahweh be great!”

And I am poor and needy;
the Lord thinks of me.
You are my help and my deliverer;
my God, do not delay.

Yahweh will guard him and will keep him alive,
and he will be called happy in the land;
so do not give him into the soul of his enemies.

And if he comes to see me, he speaks worthlessness;
his heart gathers iniquity to itself.
He goes out to the outside; he speaks.

Your arrows are sharp;
the peoples fall under you;
in the heart of the enemies of the king.

making wars cease to the end of the earth.
He shatters the bow and cuts the spear in pieces;
he burns the wagons with fire.

Let Mount Zion rejoice,
let the daughters of Judah be glad,
because of your judgments.

“Hear, my people, and I will speak;
Israel, and I will testify against you.
I am God, your God.

“Behold, the man did not make God his refuge,
but he trusted in the abundance of his wealth;
he was strong in his calamity.”

For an enemy does not reproach me;
then I would bear it.
One hating me has not made great against me;
then I would hide myself from him.

May desolations be upon them;
may they go down to Sheol alive,
for evils are in their dwelling,
in the midst of them.

Evening and morning and noon,
let me complain and moan,
and he will hear my voice.

They prepare a net for my steps;
my soul bows down.
They dig a pit to my face;
they fall into the midst of it. Selah

God has spoken in his holiness,
“I will rejoice;
I divide Shechem and measure out the Valley of Succoth.

But the king will rejoice in God;
all of the swearers by him will exult,
for the mouth of speakers of falsehood will be shut.

They strengthen for themselves an evil matter;
they recount hiding snares.
They say, “Who will see them?”

You visit the earth and saturate it;
you greatly enrich it.
The channel of God is full of water;
you prepare their grain,
for thus you prepare it.

All of the earth bows down to you
and makes music to you;
they make music to your name.” Selah

He turned the sea into dry land;
they passed through the river on foot.
There let us rejoice in him!

He is ruling by his might forever;
his eyes watch over the nations.
Let the ones rebelling not exalt themselves. Selah

You made man ride over our head;
we went through fire and through waters,
but you brought us out to abundance.

I will offer up burnt offerings of fatlings to you
with the smoke of rams;
I will offer cattle with male goats. Selah

May the nations rejoice and shout joyfully,
for you judge the peoples with uprightness,
and the nations on the earth, you guide them. Selah

As smoke is driven away, drive them away;
as wax melts from the face of fire,
let the wicked perish from the face of God.

God is making the lonely dwell in a house;
he is bringing out prisoners into prosperity.
But the ones rebelling dwell in dryness.

the earth quaked; indeed, the heavens dripped
from the face of God;
this Sinai, from the face of God, the God of Israel.

There is Benjamin, the littlest,
ruling them; the princes of Judah, their throngs;
the princes of Zebulun, the princes of Naphtali.

Ascribe strength to God;
his majesty is over Israel,
and his strength is in the clouds.

But I am poor and needy;
God, hurry to me!
You are my help and my deliverer;
Yahweh, do not delay!

Be to me a rock of abode for coming continually;
you command to save me,
for you are my rock and my stronghold.

I have supported myself on you from the womb;
you were taking me from the belly of my mother.
My praise is about you continually.

saying, “God has forsaken him;
pursue and seize him,
for there is none delivering.”

For your righteousness, God, is to height,
you who do great things;
God, who is like you?

Also I, I will praise you with the instrument of the lute
for your faithfulness, my God;
Let me make music to you with the harp, Holy One of Israel.

May he judge the poor of the people;
may he save the sons of the needy,
and may he crush the oppressor.

May he live! And may one give to him from the gold of Sheba,
and may one pray for him continually;
may they bless him all of the day.

May there be an abundance of grain in the land;
on the head of the mountains may its fruit sway like Lebanon,
and may they flourish from the city like the grass of the earth.

May his name be forever;
may his name continue to the face of the sun.
And may they be blessed by him;
may all of the nations acclaim him.

We do not see our signs;
there is no longer a prophet
and not one with us knowing until when.

We give thanks to you, God;
we give thanks, and your name is near;
they recount your wonders.

For a cup is in the hand of Yahweh,
and the wine foams, a full mixture,
and he pours out from this;
surely its dregs they will drain;
all the wicked of the earth will drink.

The stout of heart were plundered;
they slept their sleep,
and all of the men of strength found not their hands.

In the day of my trouble I sought the Lord;
my hand was stretched out at night, and it did not slacken.
My soul refused to be comforted.

I will remember my song in the night;
with my heart I will meditate,
and my spirit searches.

The waters saw you, God;
the waters saw you, and they trembled;
indeed the depths shook.

The clouds poured down water;
the skies gave a sound;
your arrows also flew about.

The sound of your thunder was in the whirlwind;
the lightning lit up the world;
the earth trembled and shook.

He made level a path for his anger;
he did not spare their soul from death,
and their life he gave over to the plague.

God, nations have come into your inheritance;
they have defiled the temple of your holiness;
they have made Jerusalem into heaps.

Do not remember former iniquities against us;
hasten, let your compassions meet us,
for we have become very weak.

And we, your people and the flock of your pasture,
will give thanks to you forever;
to generation and generation we will recount your praise.

In distress you called, and I delivered you;
I answered you from the secret place of thunder.
I tested you at the waters of Meribah. Selah

They do not know and they do not understand;
they walk about in darkness.
All of the foundations of the earth are shaken.

Passing through in the Valley of Baca,
they make it a spring;
the early rain also covers it with blessings.

Let me hear what God Yahweh will speak,
for he will speak peace to his people and to his faithful ones,
but let them not return to folly.

Turn to me and favor me;
give your strength to your servant,
and save the son of your female servant.

You have distanced my acquaintances from me;
you have made me abominations to them.
I am shut in, and I do not go out.

My eye mourns from affliction.
I call out to you, Yahweh, in all of the day;
I spread out my palms to you.

Then you spoke in a vision to your faithful ones and said,
“I have placed help on a warrior;
I have raised up a chosen one from the people.

May the favor of the Lord our God be upon us.
And the work of our hands, establish for us;
indeed, the work of our hands, establish it.

A thousand may fall at your side,
and a myriad at your right hand;
it will not approach toward you.

He will call me and I will answer him.
I will be with him in trouble;
I will rescue him and I will honor him.

with a ten string
and with a lyre;
with a melody on a harp.

Yahweh reigns; he wears majesty;
Yahweh wears, he girds himself with, strength.
Indeed, the world is firmly established; it cannot be moved.

The seas rise, Yahweh;
the seas have lifted up their voice;
the seas lift up their pounding waves.

Your decrees are very trustworthy;
holiness adorns your house,
Yahweh, for length of days.

Sing to Yahweh a new song,
for he has done marvelous things;
his right hand and the arm of his holiness have brought him salvation.

to the face of Yahweh who is coming to judge the earth;
he will judge the world with righteousness
and the peoples with fairness.

And the strength of the king: he loves justice.
You, you have established fairness;
you, you have done justice and righteousness in Jacob.

Know that Yahweh, he is God;
he, he made us, and not we,
his people and the sheep of his pasture.

I will not put a worthless thing before my eyes;
I hate to do transgressions;
it will not cling to me.

You, you will arise, you will have mercy on Zion;
for it is the time to favor her;
for the appointed time has come.

They, they will perish, but you, you will stand,
and all of them will wear out like a garment;
like clothing, you will pass them off, and they will pass away.

Bless Yahweh, my soul!
Yahweh my God, you are very great;
you are clothed with splendor and majesty,

the one setting his upper chambers on the waters;
the one appointing the clouds his chariot;
the one walking on the wings of the wind;

How many are your works, Yahweh!
You made all of them with wisdom;
the earth is full of your creation.

You hide your face; they are terrified;
you take away their breath; they expire
and return to their dust.

Our fathers did not consider your marvelous deeds in Egypt;
they did not remember the abundance of your covenant faithfulness,
and they rebelled at the sea, the Sea of Reeds.

And he has gathered them from lands,
from the sunrise and from the evening,
from the north and from the sea.

Moab is a tub for my washing;
over Edom I throw my sandal;
over Philistia I shout triumphantly.”

They, they will curse, but you, you will bless;
they arise, but then become ashamed,
and your servant will rejoice.

He will judge the nations;
he fills with bodies, he crushes the head,
upon abundant land.

He has sent redemption to his people;
he ordained his covenant forever;
holy and awesome is his name.

The fear of Yahweh is the beginning of wisdom;
good understanding to all those doing them.
His praise stands forever!

He scatters, he gives to the poor;
his righteousness stands forever;
his horn is high with honor.

The wicked will see and be angry;
he will grind his teeth and he will melt away;
the desire of the wicked will perish.

Hallelu Yah!
Praise him, servants of Yahweh;
praise the name of Yahweh!

Their hands, but they do not feel;
their feet, but they cannot walk;
they do not murmur in their throats.

Yahweh remembers us; he will bless;
he will bless the house of Israel;
he will bless the house of Aaron.

The cords of death surrounded me,
and the constrictions of Sheol found me;
I found anguish and sorrow.

Indeed, Yahweh, for I am your servant;
I am your servant, the son of your servant woman;
you have undone my bonds.

They surrounded me like bees;
they were extinguished like a fire of thorns;
in the name of Yahweh, indeed I fended them off.

Let the proud have shame,
for they have slandered me with a lie;
I, I will meditate on your precepts.

Yahweh, deliver my soul
from a lip of falsehood,
from a tongue of deceit.

Lord, hear my voice;
let your ears be attentive
to the voice of my supplications.

Israel, hope in Yahweh,
for with Yahweh is covenant faithfulness,
and with him is abundant redemption.

Rather, I have stilled and quieted my soul
like a weaned child upon his mother;
like a weaned child upon me is my soul.

Hallelu Yah!
Praise the name of Yahweh;
praise him, servants of Yahweh,

Though I walk in the middle of trouble, you will keep me alive;
you will stretch out your hand against the nose of my enemies,
and your right hand will save me.

Yahweh will accomplish for my benefit;
your covenant faithfulness, Yahweh, is forever.
Do not forsake the works of your hands.

Even darkness does not make it dark to you,
and the night shines like the day;
like darkness, like light.

Guard me, Yahweh, from the hands of the wicked;
from the man of violence preserve me,
who have planned to push down my steps.

The proud have hidden a snare for me, and cords;
they have spread out a net to the hand of the path;
traps they have set for me. Selah

Let burning coals fall on them;
let him cast them into the fire,
into pits, let them not rise up.

I cried out to you, Yahweh;
I said, “You are my shelter,
my portion in the land of the living.”

For the enemy has pursued my soul;
he has crushed my life to the ground;
he has made me to live in dark places
like the dead of ages.

I remember days from before;
I meditate on all your works;
I reflect on the works of your hands.

Send your hands from above;
break me free and deliver me from many waters,
from the hand of sons of a foreigner,

May our oxen be burdened;
no breach and no going out
and no cry in our squares.

Yahweh is opening the blind;
Yahweh is raising up the one bowed down;
Yahweh is loving the righteous.

Yahweh is guarding the sojourners;
he upholds the orphan and the widow,
but the way of the wicked, he overturns.

Yahweh reigns forever;
your God, Zion, to generation and generation.
Hallelu Yah!

the one covering the heavens with clouds;
the one preparing rain for the earth,
the one making the mountains sprout with grass.

Hallelu Yah!
Praise Yahweh from the heavens;
praise him in the heights.

Let them praise the name of Yahweh,
for his name alone is exalted;
his splendor is over the earth and the heavens.

Hallelu Yah!
Praise God in his sanctuary;
praise him in the expanse of his strength.
